    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d276">

                <pb facs="0406" n="324" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg324"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/3569: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ellis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-04-13T10:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 13,
                                1925—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:44
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>26. Referring to the Department’s telegram of April 11, 4 p.m. Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs assures me that his Government will do everything possible to
                    stabilize conditions on Honduras frontier. He states that General Ferrera<anchor
                        n="17" xml:id="d276-f1"/> who is now concentrated here intends to leave for
                    Mexico soon.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ellis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d276-f1" n="17" xml:id="d276-f1-content">
                <p>Gen. Gregorio Ferrera, Honduran exile in Guatemala.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
